  "id": "Compound::DB06637 - Gene::3786",
  "verbalization": "Dalfampridine is shown to interact with multiple potassium channel proteins, including Kcna6, Kcnf1, and Kcnv2, all of which are involved in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. This activity is ultimately linked to the participation of Kcnq3, a key component of the delayed rectifier potassium channel. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust relationship between Dalfampridine and Kcnq3, likely through a shared mechanism involving the modulation of potassium channel function. The evidence implies that Dalfampridine may influence Kcnq3 through a pathway that involves the delayed rectifier potassium channel, potentially by modulating the activity of its associated subunits. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of potassium channels in cellular electrophysiology and suggests that Dalfampridine could exert its effects by interacting with these channels, possibly through a mechanism that involves the Kcnq3 subunit.",
